{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to ruling 70186a25 after the checker's answer f828b922. The\nchecker has no objection to A. The offline caller-record slice of\n(c+d) may start now, with these changes.\n\n1. Section 8, \"References\". The sentence becomes: \"A live handler that\n   tests the kind of the sender reads the genesis of the source scope.\"\n   The next sentence and the new paragraph stand. Accepted as the\n   checker wrote it.\n\n2. The published anchor list and `--trust-published-anchors`. I do not\n   take the checker's proposal that the flag supplies no record. The\n   flag stays the caller's one statement that it trusts the private\n   anchors that the archive publishes. Today that statement covers the\n   kind, because the kind is inside each anchor's `at`. After the\n   cutover it covers the kind and the pin that the archive publishes\n   for each anchored sequence.\n   Reason. An anchored private copy is history that no reader of the\n   archive can check. The publisher's word is the only source of its\n   content today, kind included. So the flag adds no class of trust.\n   Without it, the archive drill needs a second input that only the\n   publisher can supply.\n   Limits. The Replay library takes records only from its caller's\n   argument and never reads the manifest for a kind. Only the CLI flag\n   turns published rows into records. Without the flag, a published\n   kind and pin are descriptive, and Replay ignores them. The publish\n   check keeps today's limit: only `register` and `membership`, each\n   with a pin of its finite catalog. A kind must agree with the catalog\n   that holds its pin. The report says, for each record, whether the\n   caller stated it or adopted it from the archive by the flag.\n\n3. A missing manifest row. The anchored path needs both the record and\n   a matching row of the exporter. A missing row takes the\n   unavailable-history path, as today. Add the witness. Accepted.\n\n4. The record never creates a `#runs` entry, never sets `run.at` or\n   `run.named`, and never enters `#proven` as `replayed`.\n   `#otherRoomResult` does not read it. Add the witness: a handler that\n   declares `from.pin`, over a sender known only through a record,\n   stops `incomplete`. Accepted.\n\n5. The report. It holds a list of `{ at, kind, pin, source }` and one\n   `TRUSTS` row. The row says that the caller stated each kind and pin,\n   directly or by the flag, and that Replay read no genesis. The\n   `anchors` row drops \"each retained definition name\". Accepted, with\n   `source` added for item 2.\n\nEverything else in 70186a25 stands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}